{
 "version": 1,
 "set": "xbla",
 "about": "N64 texture id -> the identity of the user-supplied XBLA resource that replaces it, for the 161 accepted mappings. \"bundle\" and \"res\" name a resource inside a source the USER supplies; \"flips\" are the two orientation corrections (HD->source, source->N64) applied when converting. \"n64\" is the image-table entry's width and height (imageTypes.txt). No source bytes are recorded here, Sightline neither distributes nor locates any source, and the pixel stage's review-tier candidates are deliberately absent; an id may instead be established by GEOMETRY, where a level's remastered and original backgrounds draw it on the same triangles with the same texture coordinates, or tile it on a whole number of the remaster image's own repeat cells (docs/texture-packs.md, \"Pairing by geometry\", \"Re-tiled pairs\"). An entry may also carry \"bleed\" (fill transparent texels' colour from their covered neighbours), \"level\" (scale the colour to the native image's mean luminance) and \"sample\" (resample a re-UV'd remaster item's window into the native texture's domain; tools/texpack/nativeuv.py).",
